@DaiqingChen 
Thank you for your feedback regarding the THSD4 (ADAMTSL6) annotation.
While the reference you mentioned (PMID: 23962539) uses the phrase "probably associated with microfibrils," several other reports (PMID:19940141 PMID:21880733. PMID:32855533. PMID:32141660) including more recent findings—consistently demonstrate that THSD4 is a specific protein localized within the microfibril and actively involved in microfibril dynamics... Given that some of the later studies provide a more definitive and contemporary view than the 2013 reference, should MGI keep the THSD4 (ADAMTSL6) microfibril annotation? Thanks!  Li

